<!DOCTYPE html><html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <title>Will You Be My Valentine?</title>
  <style>
    body {
      margin: 0;
      font-family: 'Segoe UI', Tahoma, Geneva, Verdana, sans-serif;
      background: linear-gradient(135deg, #ff9a9e, #fad0c4);
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      height: 100vh;
      color: #fff;
      text-align: center;
    }.card {
  background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.15);
  padding: 40px;
  border-radius: 20px;
  box-shadow: 0 10px 30px rgba(0,0,0,0.2);
  max-width: 400px;
  width: 90%;
  backdrop-filter: blur(10px);
}

h1 {
  font-size: 2.5rem;
  margin-bottom: 10px;
}

p {
  font-size: 1.2rem;
  margin-bottom: 30px;
}

.buttons {
  display: flex;
  gap: 20px;
  justify-content: center;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
}

button {
  padding: 12px 25px;
  font-size: 1rem;
  border: none;
  border-radius: 30px;
  cursor: pointer;
  transition: transform 0.2s ease, background 0.3s ease;
}

#yesBtn {
  background: #ff4b5c;
  color: white;
}

#yesBtn:hover {
  transform: scale(1.1);
  background: #ff1e38;
}

#noBtn {
  background: white;
  color: #ff4b5c;
}

#message {
  margin-top: 25px;
  font-size: 1.4rem;
  font-weight: bold;
}

  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <div class="card">
    <h1>Hey ❤️</h1>
    <p>From the moment you came into my life, everything felt brighter.
       So I have one very important question for you…</p><h1>Will you be my Valentine? 💌</h1>

<div class="buttons">
  <button id="yesBtn" onclick="sayYes()">Yes 💖</button>
  <button id="noBtn" onclick="moveNo()">No 🙈</button>
</div>

<div id="message"></div>

  </div>  <script>
    function sayYes() {
      document.getElementById('message').innerHTML = "Yayyy! ❤️ I knew you'd say yes 😘";
    }

    function moveNo() {
      const noBtn = document.getElementById('noBtn');
      const x = Math.random() * 200 - 100;
      const y = Math.random() * 200 - 100;
      noBtn.style.transform = `translate(${x}px, ${y}px)`;
    }
  </script></body>
</html>
